WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.935 --> 00:00:18.117
Mother Wolf gazed at the small human in wonder.

2
00:00:18.137 --> 00:00:20.519
"He's so little!"

3
00:00:21.179 --> 00:00:22.260
she said softly.

4
00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:26.982
The young boy was squirming between two cubs to get warm.

5
00:00:27.002 --> 00:00:29.464
"Look at that!

6
00:00:30.004 --> 00:00:31.985
He's not afraid of us or the cubs."

7
00:00:33.225 --> 00:00:37.506
"I've heard of young humans living with wolves," Father Wolf said.

8
00:00:37.526 --> 00:00:40.867
"But I've never seen it in my own pack."

9
00:00:42.407 --> 00:00:47.209
Just then the wolves heard something and spun toward the entrance of the cave.

10
00:00:48.209 --> 00:00:52.350
Tabaqui had returned—with the tiger, Shere Khan.

11
00:00:52.370 --> 00:00:55.331
"The boy is here, master!"

12
00:00:55.851 --> 00:00:57.371
the jackal said eagerly.

13
00:00:57.391 --> 00:00:59.112
"I see him."

14
00:01:02.780 --> 00:01:08.322
"Shere Khan, your visit brings us great honor," Father Wolf said politely.

15
00:01:10.103 --> 00:01:12.104
But his eyes sparked with anger.

16
00:01:12.124 --> 00:01:14.425
"What do you need?"

17
00:01:15.825 --> 00:01:19.587
"A human cub went this way," Shere Khan said.

18
00:01:19.607 --> 00:01:21.928
"His parents have run off.

19
00:01:23.028 --> 00:01:25.289
Give the man cub to me."

20
00:01:26.930 --> 00:01:31.212
Luckily, the cave entrance was too narrow for Shere Khan to enter.

21
00:01:32.444 --> 00:01:36.307
"We wolves are free creatures," said Father Wolf.

22
00:01:37.548 --> 00:01:41.091
"We take orders from the head of the pack, not from you."

23
00:01:42.172 --> 00:01:45.255
The tiger's furious roar filled the cave.

24
00:01:48.557 --> 00:01:50.199
Mother Wolf sprang forward.

25
00:01:52.280 --> 00:01:57.685
In the darkness her eyes looked like two green moons as she faced Shere Khan.

26
00:01:57.705 --> 00:01:59.726
"The human cub is mine!"

27
00:02:00.267 --> 00:02:01.088
She growled.

28
00:02:02.048 --> 00:02:03.849
"He will not be killed.

29
00:02:04.229 --> 00:02:07.531
He will live to run with the pack and to hunt with the pack.

30
00:02:07.931 --> 00:02:09.212
Now go, Shere Khan!"

31
00:02:11.393 --> 00:02:13.254
Father looked on in amazement.

32
00:02:14.275 --> 00:02:18.117
He had forgotten how fierce his mate could be when she was angry.

33
00:02:19.598 --> 00:02:21.799
Shere Khan backed away from the cave.

34
00:02:21.819 --> 00:02:26.382
"We'll see what the pack says about that human cub!"

35
00:02:26.962 --> 00:02:27.762
He snarled.

36
00:02:27.782 --> 00:02:33.594
"He's mine, and his life will end in my teeth!"

37
00:02:40.417 --> 00:02:46.001
Mother threw herself down among the cubs as Father watched the tiger stalk off.

38
00:02:46.021 --> 00:02:52.884
"Shere Khan spoke the truth about one thing," Father said with a sigh.

39
00:02:56.867 --> 00:02:58.988
must show this cub to the pack.

40
00:02:59.512 --> 00:03:01.273
Do you really plan to keep him?"

41
00:03:01.293 --> 00:03:04.055
"Of course I'll keep him!"

42
00:03:04.535 --> 00:03:05.395
Mother snapped.

43
00:03:05.415 --> 00:03:10.158
"The poor little creature came at night, alone and hungry.

44
00:03:11.118 --> 00:03:13.420
I'll call him Mowgli," she added.

45
00:03:13.440 --> 00:03:19.283
"One day he will hunt Shere Khan, just as that tiger has hunted him."

46
00:03:20.583 --> 00:03:21.704
Father was worried.

47
00:03:21.724 --> 00:03:24.085
"What will our pack say?"

48
00:03:25.166 --> 00:03:27.467
The law of the jungle was very clear.

49
00:03:30.644 --> 00:03:35.026
The pack protected young cubs until they were old enough to hunt on their own.

50
00:03:37.567 --> 00:03:40.748
But the pack wasn't likely to protect a human cub.

51
00:03:40.768 --> 00:03:45.990
"We'll deal with that later," Mother replied firmly.

52
00:03:46.671 --> 00:03:50.412
The pack council met once every month, when the moon was full.

53
00:03:51.132 --> 00:03:55.254
It was the duty of all new parents to show their cubs to the council.

54
00:03:57.715 --> 00:04:02.433
On the night of the next pack meeting, Father and Mother went to Council Rock.

55
00:04:03.774 --> 00:04:06.235
The wolf cubs and Mowgli ran after them.

56
00:04:09.916 --> 00:04:13.778
Council Rock was a hilltop covered with stones and boulders.

57
00:04:15.278 --> 00:04:19.400
Akela, the great gray wolf, lay across a rock.

58
00:04:20.361 --> 00:04:22.401
He had led the pack for a year now.

59
00:04:23.602 --> 00:04:28.264
He was a wise, strong leader, who knew the ways and customs of people.

60
00:04:29.500 --> 00:04:31.562
It was very quiet at Council Rock.

61
00:04:32.543 --> 00:04:34.364
All the parents sat in a circle.

62
00:04:35.645 --> 00:04:40.069
In the center of the circle, the cubs tumbled over one another, playing.

63
00:04:41.230 --> 00:04:44.953
One by one, the wolf parents showed their cubs to the pack.

64
00:04:47.114 --> 00:04:49.036
"Look well, oh, wolves!"

65
00:04:49.516 --> 00:04:50.397
Akela cried.

66
00:04:52.098 --> 00:04:54.580
The mothers anxiously repeated the call.

67
00:04:54.600 --> 00:04:58.303
"Look, look well, oh, wolves!"

68
00:05:01.240 --> 00:05:02.581
Mother's fur quivered.

69
00:05:03.381 --> 00:05:06.162
It was almost time to show Mowgli to the pack.

70
00:05:07.103 --> 00:05:11.385
What would the wolves say when they saw the odd-looking man cub?
